WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:27.020 --> 00:00:31.440
[Narrator:] The designation HeLa refers to
the name of

00:00:31.440 --> 00:00:35.400
a patient who was operated for the treatment

00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:38.400
of a cervical carcinoma.

00:00:57.199 --> 00:01:03.099
[Narrator:] Dr. and Mrs. George Guy of the
Johns Hopkins Hospital

00:01:03.100 --> 00:01:08.300
in Baltimore established this cell strain
which has been

00:01:08.310 --> 00:01:13.360
in continuous culture since nineteen-hundred
and fifty-one.

00:01:13.360 --> 00:01:18.220
HeLa cells are grown in test tubes where

00:01:18.220 --> 00:01:24.320
they may be harvested from the walls by means of
a rubber policeman.

00:01:24.320 --> 00:01:28.620
The colonies are collected in petri dishes

00:01:28.630 --> 00:01:31.869
containing nutrient fluid.

00:01:31.869 --> 00:01:35.319
They are transferred later to the surface

00:01:35.319 --> 00:01:41.640
of a large sterile glass slide and cut into
fragments

00:01:41.640 --> 00:01:50.280
suitable for subculture in bottles, test tubes, or on cover slips.

00:01:50.280 --> 00:01:52.960
Cells are stimulated by cutting,

00:01:52.969 --> 00:01:54.889
but this must be done

00:01:54.889 --> 00:01:59.509
with sharp knives to avoid excess trauma.

00:02:03.060 --> 00:02:07.560
The cut fragments are collected in a petri
dish

00:02:07.569 --> 00:02:11.389
containing a nutrient solution.

00:02:18.280 --> 00:02:22.820
The essential steps in preparing a culture
are now shown.

00:02:22.820 --> 00:02:25.819
Cover glasses are placed on a slide,

00:02:25.819 --> 00:02:29.479
and plasma is dropped on their surface.

00:02:29.480 --> 00:02:35.820
The tissues are now picked up on the tip of
a knife blade

00:02:35.820 --> 00:02:39.440
and are transferred to the plasma.

00:02:40.340 --> 00:02:45.660
They are placed at equidistant points on the
cover glass.

00:02:48.700 --> 00:02:53.040
An equal amount of embryonic extract is added,

00:02:53.040 --> 00:02:55.140
and the mixture is stirred.

00:02:55.150 --> 00:03:01.630
When the clot is set, each slide is placed
in a test tube,

00:03:01.630 --> 00:03:04.430
fluid nutrient is added,

00:03:04.430 --> 00:03:08.830
and the culture is incubated at body temperature.

00:03:12.840 --> 00:03:18.060
Here we see the development of a freshly transferred culture,

00:03:18.060 --> 00:03:21.300
photographed at one frame per minute.

00:03:21.310 --> 00:03:23.470
Notice the frame counter

00:03:23.470 --> 00:03:26.040
in the right-hand portion of the field.

00:03:26.050 --> 00:03:31.570
The middle number represents the flight of
time in minutes.

00:03:31.570 --> 00:03:35.020
Since this portion of the film was photographed

00:03:35.020 --> 00:03:37.190
at one frame per minute,

00:03:37.190 --> 00:03:41.840
and is being projected at 24 frames per second,

00:03:41.840 --> 00:03:46.320
what we see on the screen is accelerated

00:03:46.320 --> 00:03:51.260
by a factor of more than 1,000 times.

00:03:51.260 --> 00:03:56.180
The colony spreads with characteristic shifting
motions

00:03:56.180 --> 00:03:58.600
of the cells.

00:03:58.600 --> 00:04:03.120
At higher magnification we see the advance

00:04:03.120 --> 00:04:06.880
of the margin of the outgrowing cells.

00:04:14.640 --> 00:04:18.140
Three arrows point to rotating nuclei,

00:04:18.150 --> 00:04:23.110
a curious phenomenon encountered in tissue
cultures

00:04:23.110 --> 00:04:26.340
studied with time-lapse photography.

00:04:26.340 --> 00:04:28.560
At higher magnification,

00:04:28.560 --> 00:04:33.760
we see a nuclear rotation in an individual
cell.

00:04:34.480 --> 00:04:40.680
This portion of the record is accelerated
160 times.

00:04:46.140 --> 00:04:53.060
Then the speed is increased to more than 1,000
times

00:04:53.060 --> 00:04:56.200
in order to dramatize the effect.

00:05:01.800 --> 00:05:06.760
Mitoses of normal and abnormal types are common.

00:05:06.760 --> 00:05:10.480
Three arrows locate elements which will show

00:05:10.490 --> 00:05:13.410
normal bipolar divisions,

00:05:13.410 --> 00:05:16.480
and a single arrow points to a cell

00:05:16.480 --> 00:05:21.320
which will produce a tripolar mitosis.

00:05:25.960 --> 00:05:29.960
Here is a quadripolar mitosis.

00:05:29.960 --> 00:05:36.060
Frequently, abnormalities of the spindle can
be seen.

00:05:36.060 --> 00:05:42.900
Chromosomal movements show a wide variety
of derangements.

00:05:42.900 --> 00:05:50.140
The number of chromosomes is generally between
80 and 90,

00:05:50.140 --> 00:05:57.840
but sometimes more than 200 chromosomes can
be demonstrated

00:05:57.840 --> 00:06:02.780
in dividing cells of the HeLa strain.

00:06:05.500 --> 00:06:10.180
Two nuclei are seen in this giant cell,

00:06:11.760 --> 00:06:17.060
and here is a giant cell with multiple nuclei

00:06:17.060 --> 00:06:21.800
which appears to be in the process of degeneration.

00:06:23.880 --> 00:06:27.200
This portion of the film shows numerous

00:06:27.210 --> 00:06:31.050
threadlike cytoplasmic processes.

00:06:31.050 --> 00:06:36.550
Such filopodia are typical of the HeLa cell.

00:06:36.550 --> 00:06:41.280
We see them in a sequence where the level
of focus

00:06:41.280 --> 00:06:47.280
was changed to show their arrangement in patches.

00:06:47.280 --> 00:06:50.460
In the right-hand portion of this field,

00:06:50.460 --> 00:06:57.480
the pattern is found even over the area of
the nucleus.

00:07:05.340 --> 00:07:10.340
In situ, filopodia probably are associated

00:07:10.340 --> 00:07:14.100
in an interplay between neighboring cells.

00:07:14.100 --> 00:07:18.660
Here we can see the movements of intercellular
strands

00:07:18.660 --> 00:07:22.260
between two cells in vitro.

00:07:23.300 --> 00:07:29.660
In addition to the surface activity of the
threadlike processes,

00:07:29.660 --> 00:07:34.500
the cytoplasm often shows characteristic ruffles,

00:07:34.500 --> 00:07:41.620
which lead to the engulfment of nutrient fluid
invacuoles.

00:07:41.620 --> 00:07:47.680
This process is very commonly found in HeLa
cultures.

00:07:47.680 --> 00:07:49.880
We see it taking place

00:07:49.880 --> 00:07:53.180
in the left-hand portion of the field.

00:07:53.180 --> 00:07:56.720
We can also observe twitching movements

00:07:56.720 --> 00:08:01.080
of the cytoplasm, which remain unexplained.

00:08:01.080 --> 00:08:04.919
This sequence and many others were collected

00:08:04.919 --> 00:08:07.679
in the course of investigations

00:08:07.679 --> 00:08:11.599
on the behavior of the HeLa cell as a part

00:08:11.600 --> 00:08:15.440
of a cancer research program.

00:08:21.500 --> 00:08:26.080
Cell drinking, or pinocytosis, as described

00:08:26.080 --> 00:08:30.290
by Dr. Warren Lewis many years ago, accounts

00:08:30.290 --> 00:08:34.820
for the intake of large quantities of nutrients.

00:08:35.640 --> 00:08:40.040
Cells of this type may ingest more than one
third

00:08:40.050 --> 00:08:43.269
of their volume in one hour.

00:08:43.269 --> 00:08:48.430
The mechanism of pinocytosis and its consequences

00:08:48.430 --> 00:08:51.350
remains one of the most challenging problems

00:08:51.350 --> 00:08:54.250
of cell physiology.

00:08:57.260 --> 00:09:01.920
These records show nutrient intake at the
margin,

00:09:01.920 --> 00:09:06.640
and the migration of fluid vacuoles toward
the nucleus.

00:09:08.020 --> 00:09:10.360
These fields were photographed

00:09:10.360 --> 00:09:13.560
with an oil immersion objective.

00:09:26.280 --> 00:09:30.300
Active folds on the surface of cells

00:09:30.310 --> 00:09:35.570
lead some observers to believe that this may
result

00:09:35.570 --> 00:09:38.649
in the formation of mitochondria.

00:09:39.400 --> 00:09:43.780
However, at a slightly deeper level of focus,

00:09:43.789 --> 00:09:46.740
we see that filamentous mitochondria

00:09:46.740 --> 00:09:50.440
are quite different from the folds at the
surface.

00:09:50.440 --> 00:09:53.560
The view of an entire cell photographed

00:09:53.560 --> 00:09:56.140
with phase-contrast optics

00:09:56.140 --> 00:10:02.130
shows cell organs such as mitochondria, vacuoles,

00:10:02.130 --> 00:10:07.830
and lipoprotein granules grouped in characteristic
patterns.

00:10:07.830 --> 00:10:12.660
The juxtanuclear zone or Golgi apparatus,

00:10:12.670 --> 00:10:16.430
as it is described from fixed preparations,

00:10:16.430 --> 00:10:20.890
is probably represented here in the aggregation

00:10:20.890 --> 00:10:24.710
of various cell organoids.

00:10:26.300 --> 00:10:34.240
The HeLa cell has become a very useful material
for experimental work

00:10:34.250 --> 00:10:40.830
not only in the study of cancer but in the
field of general cytology.

00:10:40.830 --> 00:10:47.190
It is easily cultivated, it exhibits many
abnormalities,

00:10:47.190 --> 00:10:54.330
and is valuable for the cultivation of a wide
variety of viruses.

